['Here is your Java solution based on your description using Semaphores for managing resources and ExecutorService for managing threads:

```java
import java.util.Random;
import java.util.concurrent.*;
import java.util.logging.*;

public class Main {
    private static final Logger LOGGER = Logger.getLogger(Main.class.getName());
    private static Semaphore semaphore = new Semaphore(5); // 5 services available initially
    private static ExecutorService executor = Executors.newCachedThreadPool();
    private static Random random = new Random();

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) { // start 10 services
            executor.execute(() -> {
                try {
                    LOGGER.info("Service is waiting to acquire semaphore");
                    semaphore.acquire();
                    LOGGER.info("Service acquired semaphore");

                    int delay = random.nextInt(1000); // random delay between 0 and 999 ms
                    Thread.sleep(delay); // simulate service work

                    semaphore.release();
                    LOGGER.info("Service released semaphore after " + delay + "ms");
                } catch (InterruptedException e) {
                    Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
                } finally {
                    LOGGER.info("Service sent message to messaging system");
                }
            });
        }

        executor.shutdown();
    }
}
```
This program starts 10 services, each represented by a Runnable task that is submitted to an ExecutorService for concurrent execution. The semaphore.acquire() call blocks until a permit is available, and then it acquires the permit. When the service finishes its work, it releases the permit with semaphore.release().

Please note that this is a simplified example without real messaging system integration, you would need to implement this part yourself according to your specific requirements. Also, please don't forget to handle possible exceptions in your production code.
