['Here is your Java program:

```java
import java.io.*;
import java.nio.file.*;

public class Main {
    private static final String TEMP_DIR = System.getProperty("java.io.tmpdir");
    private static final int TIMEOUT = 10 * 60 * 1000; // Timeout in milliseconds

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        File tempDir = new File(TEMP_DIR);
        if (!tempDir.exists()) tempDir.mkdir();

        try (TemporaryFile temporaryFile = new TemporaryFile(tempDir)) {
            Process process = Runtime.getRuntime().exec("command", null, tempDir);

            long startTime = System.currentTimeMillis();
            int exitValue = process.waitFor();
            if ((System.currentTimeMillis() - startTime) > TIMEOUT) {
                process.destroy();
            } else {
                // Logging standard output and error streams to log files
                try (BufferedReader inputReader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(process.getInputStream()));
                     PrintWriter stdOutLog = new PrintWriter(new FileOutputStream("stdout_log", true));
                     BufferedReader errorReader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(process.getErrorStream()));
                     PrintWriter errOutLog = new PrintWriter(new FileOutputStream("stderr_log", true))) {

                    String line;
                    while ((line = inputReader.readLine()) != null) stdOutLog.println(line);
                    while ((line = errorReader.readLine()) != null) errOutLog.println(line);
                } catch (IOException e) {
                    System.err.println("Error logging output: " + e.getMessage());
                }
            }

        } catch (Exception e) {
            System.err.println("Error executing command: " + e.getMessage());
        }
    }

    private static class TemporaryFile implements AutoCloseable {
        private final File file;

        public TemporaryFile(File directory) throws IOException {
            file = File.createTempFile("prefix", null, directory);
            // Set permissions if needed
            setReadable(true).setWritable(true); 
        }

        @Override
        public void close() throws Exception {
            if (file != null) Files.deleteIfExists(file.toPath());
        }

        // Helper methods to adjust permissions
        private TemporaryFile setReadable(boolean readable) {
            file.setReadable(readable);
            return this;
        }

        private TemporaryFile setWritable(boolean writable) {
            file.setWritable(writable);
            return this;
        }
    }
}
```
This program creates a temporary directory and a temporary file inside it, and deletes the file after execution of the command "command". The output and error streams of the executed command are logged to stdout_log and stderr_log files respectively. If the command takes more than 10 minutes (TIMEOUT), the process is destroyed.

Please replace `"command"` with your actual command in the `Runtime.getRuntime().exec()` method.

The logging service integration, exception handling, and other aspects of this program can be further enhanced depending on specific requirements or constraints.
