generateSequence(session, sequence16, 16);
// Do something with sequence16
endSession(session);
cleanupRandom();
```
Please note that the above code does not handle concurrent calls. If you want to support concurrent calls, consider using a locking mechanism like pthread mutexes or semaphores to protect access to the `sessions` array and other shared state variables. 

Also keep in mind that there's no built-in way to prevent sequences from being reused within the same session as it requires explicit tracking of sequence usage, which can be complex depending on your needs. You might want to consider an existing library that provides this functionality if you don't want to implement it yourself. 

Remember to use these functions with caution and always keep the OpenSSL library up-to-date due to security reasons.
