['Here is your Java program according to your instructions:

```java
import java.util.concurrent.*;
import java.util.logging.*;
import java.time.*;

public class SemaphoreManager {
    private static final Logger logger = Logger.getLogger(SemaphoreManager.class.getName());

    private Semaphore semaphore;
    private ScheduledExecutorService executorService;

    public SemaphoreManager() {
        int availableProcessors = Runtime.getRuntime().availableProcessors();
        this.semaphore = new Semaphore(availableProcessors, true);
        this.executorService = Executors.newScheduledThreadPool(availableProcessors * 2);
    }

    public void startService(String serviceName, int delayInSeconds) {
        executorService.schedule(() -> {
            try {
                semaphore.acquire();
                logger.info("Acquired semaphore for " + serviceName);
                Thread.sleep((long)(Math.random() * 1000)); // simulate work
            } catch (InterruptedException e) {
                Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
                logger.log(Level.SEVERE, "Interrupted while acquiring semaphore for " + serviceName, e);
            } finally {
                if (semaphore.availablePermits() < semaphore.getQueueLength()) {
                    // notify about service health problem 
                    logger.warning("Service " + serviceName + " is not responding within acceptable timeframe");
                }
                semaphore.release();
            }
        }, delayInSeconds, TimeUnit.SECONDS);
    }

    public void stopService(String serviceName, int minimumRunningTime) {
        executorService.schedule(() -> {
            long start = System.currentTimeMillis();
            try {
                semaphore.acquire();
                logger.info("Acquired semaphore for " + serviceName);
                Thread.sleep((long)(Math.random() * 1000)); // simulate work
                long runningTime = System.currentTimeMillis() - start;

                if (runningTime >= minimumRunningTime) {
                    // send message to messaging system
                    logger.info("Service " + serviceName + " has been running for at least " + minimumRunningTime + " ms, sending message");
                } else {
                    logger.info("Service " + serviceName + " was only running for " + runningTime + " ms, no message sent");
                }
            } catch (InterruptedException e) {
                Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
                logger.log(Level.SEVERE, "Interrupted while acquiring semaphore for " + serviceName, e);
            } finally {
                if (semaphore.availablePermits() < semaphore.getQueueLength()) {
                    // notify about service health problem 
                    logger.warning("Service " + serviceName + " is not responding within acceptable timeframe");
                }
                semaphore.release();
            }
        }, minimumRunningTime, TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS);
    }
}
```
Please note that the messaging system and alerting feature are not implemented in this code because it requires more specific information such as which message system to use or how to notify about health issues etc. 

Also, I assumed that you can just call `startService` and `stopService` methods when you need to start or stop a service respectively, but please adjust the implementation according to your needs.
