    public function __construct($hashAlgorithm = 'md5', $charSet = 'abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789', $logFilePath = 'error.log') {
        $this->hashAlgorithm = $hashAlgorithm;
        $this->charSet = $charSet;
        $this->logFilePath = $logFilePath;
    }

    public function generateRandomString($length = 10) {
        $randomString = '';
        for ($i = 0; $i < $length; $i++) {
            $index = mt_rand(0, strlen($this->charSet) - 1);
            $randomString .= $this->charSet[$index];
        }
        return $randomString;
    }

    public function hashPassword($password) {
        $hashedPassword = hash($this->hashAlgorithm, $password);
        if ($hashedPassword === false) {
            $this->logError("Failed to hash password");
            return null;
        }
        return $hashedPassword;
    }

    public function processFileInChunks($filePath) {
        $hashContext = hash_init($this->hashAlgorithm);

        $handle = fopen($filePath, "rb");
        if ($handle === false) {
            $this->logError("Failed to open file: $filePath");
            return null;
        }

        while (!feof($handle)) {
            $data = fread($handle, 8192); // Read in chunks of 8KB
            hash_update($hashContext, $data);

            // Allow other PHP scripts to run during this loop without causing the script to hang.
            session_write_close();
        }
        $md5Hash = hash_final($hashContext);

        fclose($handle);

        return $md5Hash;
    }

    public function logError($message) {
        file_put_contents($this->logFilePath, date('Y-m-d H:i:s') . " - $message\n", FILE_APPEND);
    }
}
?>
```
This class generates random strings and hashes passwords with a configurable hash algorithm. It handles file processing by reading the file in chunks to avoid loading the entire file into memory, which can be costly for large files. The class also logs errors to a specified log file path. 

Please note that you might need to adjust the code according to your specific needs and constraints. For example, if there are specific constraints about security such as preventing timing attacks or using a more secure algorithm, those would need to be taken into account when implementing this class. 

