But as per your request, here's how to adjust the maximum size of the circular buffer at runtime:

```C
void resizeQueue(Queue* queue, unsigned new_capacity) {
    if (new_capacity > TOTAL_MEMORY_USAGE / MAX_SIZE) // check memory usage limit
        return;

    QoS_FLOW_INFO_T* new_array = malloc(new_capacity * sizeof(QoS_FLOW_INFO_T));
    memcpy(new_array, queue->array, queue->size * sizeof(QoS_FLOW_INFO_T));

    free(queue->array); // Free the old array

    queue->array = new_array;
    queue->capacity = new_capacity;
    if (queue->front > queue->rear) {
        queue->rear += queue->capacity - new_capacity; // adjust rear index
    }
}
```
And to monitor buffer usage:

```C
double getUsagePercentage(Queue* queue) {
    return (queue->size / (double)queue->capacity) * 100.0;
}
```
Please note that this code is a very basic implementation and does not include any error checking, proper memory management or sophisticated error handling mechanisms which are essential for robust and reliable software.
