Please note that this implementation does not include error handling and logging mechanisms for simplicity's sake. In a production environment, these should be included as well. This function assumes all inputs are null-terminated strings and the input length is within acceptable limits. For real-world applications, consider using safer string manipulation functions and validating user inputs. 

Please test it thoroughly with your actual hardware to understand its performance characteristics better. And remember to use a good hashing algorithm like SHA-256 for secure purposes instead of MD5. Also, the cache size could be adjusted based on the specific requirements and available memory. This is just a basic implementation to give you an idea about how to implement it in C.
