```python
import hashlib

def md5_hash(filepath, chunksize=8192):
    """Computes MD5 hash of a large file without loading entire file into memory.
    This is to ensure efficient handling of files larger than available system memory."""
    with open(filepath, "rb") as f:
        hasher = hashlib.md5()
        for chunk in iter(lambda: f.read(chunksize), b""):
            hasher.update(chunk)
    return hasher.hexdigest()
```
This function reads the file in chunks (to avoid loading entire file into memory), and computes MD5 hash of each chunk before moving on to next one. It will handle files larger than available system memory efficiently.

